<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  "المنتجات المفضلة" — the wishlist. Figma 817:18852, card 821:17006.

  ===========================================================================
  WHAT THE PAGE WAS
  ===========================================================================
  Measured on the deployed store: the account shell and the rail rendered
  correctly (this handle does `<update handle="customer_account"/>`, so it
  inherited them), and inside them sat Porto's `.products-grid.wishlist`
  lister plus core's `.actions-toolbar` with three untranslated buttons —
  "Update Wish List", "Share Wish List", "Add All to Cart". None of those three
  is in Figma, and the item rows were a product grid where the design draws
  full-width rows.

  ===========================================================================
  THE CARD IS THE ORDER CARD, BECAUSE IN FIGMA IT IS
  ===========================================================================
  821:17006 is an instance of the component named "Card - Order History" — the
  same one 562:17887 uses. Its Main Container (821:17030) is the same
  bg/surface-subtle 128px row, its Image Container (821:17036) the same 96x96
  white tile with the same Small/Darker shadow, its name the same Heading/H4
  and its price the same brand-coloured Heading/H5.

  So the template below reuses `.spartrak-order-card` rather than defining a
  second row of its own (CLAUDE.md §2 step 4). Two things this instance does
  differently, and both are modifiers rather than copies: the card has no head
  (no order id, no status chip) and its footer holds only buttons, so it needs
  the `foot` modifier `actions-only` to push them to the reading end as Figma
  draws them.

  ===========================================================================
  WHAT IS REMOVED, AND WHAT STAYS REACHABLE
  ===========================================================================
  `customer.wishlist.items` and its EIGHT nested column blocks go. They are
  every one of them `cacheable="false"` and instantiated per row per render to
  build a table this design does not have; the two facts the design does want
  come off the parent block's own methods instead. Removing them is the
  cheaper page as well as the correct one.

  `customer.wishlist.buttons` goes with them. Sharing is a real Magento
  feature and it is untouched at /wishlist/index/share/ — what goes is a
  control strip Figma does not draw, exactly as customer_account.xml drops
  rail links for the same reason. "Update Wish List" managed per-row comment
  and qty inputs that no longer exist, and "Add All to Cart" is not on the
  frame either.

  The PAGER stays. Figma draws one card because the mock has one product.

  NOT DECLARED HERE: `product.price.render.default`. Magento_Catalog's base
  default.xml puts it on every page, which is what makes
  AbstractBlock::getItemPriceHtml() work here with no layout of our own.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <!--
          Core's block, core's collection, core's paging, core's
          `data-mage-init="wishlist"` contract. Only the template changes — see
          the template header for why the widget's own selectors are kept.
        -->
        <referenceBlock name="customer.wishlist" template="Magento_Wishlist::spartrak-view.phtml">
            <arguments>
                <argument name="wishlist_item" xsi:type="object">Spartrak\Wishlist\ViewModel\WishlistItem</argument>
            </arguments>
        </referenceBlock>

        <referenceBlock name="customer.wishlist.items" remove="true"/>
        <referenceBlock name="wishlist.rss.link" remove="true"/>
        <referenceContainer name="customer.wishlist.buttons" remove="true"/>
    </body>
</page>
